  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Friday)\nIssued at 125 AM CDT Sat Sep 26 2026\n\nSub-tropical jet coming off the Pacific will bring increasing \namounts of moisture, including the remnants of Hurricane Polo north \nand northeast ahead of strengthening western trough. This will allow \nprecip chances to increase beginning Tuesday. \n\nThe 00Z GFS has come in more in line with the Euro in a much slower \neastward progression of the upper low through the southwest into the \nsouthern Plains this week. After the initial increase in precip \nchances Tuesday, abundant deep layer moisture and the slow movement \nof the upper low will bring an extended chance of rain through the \nremainder of the week and perhaps into next weekend. I'm reluctant \nto say this, but this would bring in the possibility of an increased \nchance of flooding rainfall, believe it or not as we go through the \nweek, with very little chance of severe storms.",
